/target

# `nunki` keeps a project's tooling at `~/.nunki/<project>/`, never in the
# project itself: `nunki.yaml`, the HQ, and the stack fragments the slots
# mount. A copy committed here is a second copy nothing reads, and it goes
# stale without saying so — measured 2026-09-23, four of the six files left
# in `.nunki/stacks/rust/` differed from the live ones and four more were
# missing entirely.
/.nunki/
/nunki.yaml
